  ],
  "text": "Cheese, bread, coffee, chocolate, soy sauce, pickles. All of them are something rotting on purpose. Rot is only what you call it when it goes the way you did not want. Fermentation is the same process, steered. Microbes eat the sugars and hand back acids, alcohol and gas. The acid is what stops anything worse moving in. That is the preservation half. But flavour is the real prize, and it is not in the ingredient at all. Those compounds do not exist until something has eaten it first. There is no such thing as unfermented chocolate that tastes like chocolate. And humans worked all of this out thousands of years before anyone knew microbes existed. We were running biotechnology blind, and we got extremely good at it. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
